WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.779 --> 00:00:16.623
While the Darling family was happily hugging upstairs, the Lost Boys were waiting outside.

2
00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:23.708
Wendy needed time to tell her parents about them, so the boys counted to five hundred before knocking

3
00:00:23.768 --> 00:00:24.569
on the front door.

4
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.692
They thought this was more polite than flying through the window.

5
00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:31.052
When Mr.

6
00:00:31.112 --> 00:00:31.492
and Mrs.

7
00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:36.694
Darling opened the door, the boys stood in a row, looking as innocent as they could.

8
00:00:37.874 --> 00:00:41.855
Each had a sweet grin on his face and an eager spark in his eyes.

9
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:47.477
"We are very pleased to meet you," the boys said together.

10
00:00:48.717 --> 00:00:50.218
All their attention was on Mrs.

11
00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:53.379
Darling, for they hoped she would be their new mother.

12
00:00:54.639 --> 00:00:57.460
Of course she told the boys right away that she would adopt them.

13
00:00:58.508 --> 00:00:58.988
But Mr.

14
00:00:59.028 --> 00:01:01.110
Darling did not feel quite the same way.

15
00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:06.753
"Six new children is an awfully large number," he said, worried.

16
00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:09.214
"It will be very expensive."

17
00:01:10.575 --> 00:01:12.216
"George!" Mrs.

18
00:01:12.276 --> 00:01:15.798
Darling cried, upset to see his selfishness come out again.

19
00:01:16.858 --> 00:01:17.339
Then Mr.

20
00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:18.820
Darling burst into a smile.

21
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.101
He was as glad to have them as she was.

22
00:01:22.121 --> 00:01:26.344
"I just thought you could have asked my permission," he said.

23
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.584
The boys all told him that having a father was just as important as having a mother.

24
00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:35.006
Delighted, Mr.

25
00:01:35.046 --> 00:01:37.988
Darling said that he would find space for them in an extra room.

26
00:01:38.008 --> 00:01:43.493
"We can all fit into a single bed, sir," Tootles assured him.

27
00:01:44.794 --> 00:01:46.955
"Then follow me," Mr.

28
00:01:46.996 --> 00:01:48.357
Darling cried merrily.

29
00:01:48.377 --> 00:01:54.362
"Mind you, I'm not sure that we have an extra room, but we can pretend to have one."

30
00:01:55.302 --> 00:01:58.889
He went off dancing through the house, and the boys danced after him.

31
00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:04.152
As for Peter, before he flew away, he saw Wendy once more.

32
00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:10.835
She called to him from the nursery, and he shyly brushed up against the window.

33
00:02:10.855 --> 00:02:15.958
"Peter, are you really going away?"

34
00:02:16.638 --> 00:02:17.179
she asked.

35
00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:18.680
"Yes, Wendy.

36
00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.481
It's time for me to go," he said.

37
00:02:22.381 --> 00:02:25.463
"Peter, don't you want to ask my parents something?"

38
00:02:26.143 --> 00:02:26.824
Wendy asked.

39
00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.961
"No, what would I ask?"

40
00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:32.882
he answered, trying to sound casual.

41
00:02:34.042 --> 00:02:35.823
Mrs. Darling joined them at the window.

42
00:02:36.844 --> 00:02:41.185
When she saw Peter, she told him she would be happy to adopt him as well.

43
00:02:41.205 --> 00:02:44.487
"Would you send me to school?"

44
00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:45.647
he asked.

45
00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:50.509
"Yes." "And then to work?"

46
00:02:50.529 --> 00:02:51.469
"I suppose so."

47
00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:54.391
"Soon I would become a grown-up?"

48
00:02:54.871 --> 00:02:55.411
he asked.

49
00:02:55.431 --> 00:02:58.600
"Very soon," said Mrs.

50
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:04.222
Darling. "I don't want to go to school, and I don't want to be a grown-up—ever!"

51
00:03:04.782 --> 00:03:05.762
Peter protested.

52
00:03:05.782 --> 00:03:09.423
"No one is going to catch me and make me grow up."

53
00:03:09.443 --> 00:03:12.724
"But where will you live?"

54
00:03:13.464 --> 00:03:13.985
asked Mrs.

55
00:03:14.045 --> 00:03:15.085
Darling gently.

56
00:03:16.045 --> 00:03:18.666
"With Tink, in the house we built for Wendy.

57
00:03:19.506 --> 00:03:22.167
The fairies will put it up high among the treetops."

58
00:03:23.047 --> 00:03:26.068
"How lovely," said Wendy longingly.

59
00:03:27.328 --> 00:03:30.290
"I thought all the fairies were dead," said Mrs.

60
00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:37.014
Darling. "There are always more young ones," explained Wendy, who was now an expert on fairies.

61
00:03:38.014 --> 00:03:39.535
"I shall have such fun!"

62
00:03:40.115 --> 00:03:41.356
said Peter to Wendy.

63
00:03:41.376 --> 00:03:48.360
"But it will be so lonely in the evenings sitting by the fire," Wendy said sadly.

64
00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:52.102
"Well then, come with me," he said.

65
00:03:52.122 --> 00:03:53.623
"May I, Mother?"

66
00:03:54.203 --> 00:03:54.864
Wendy asked.

67
00:03:56.216 --> 00:03:58.237
"Certainly not," Mrs.

68
00:03:58.277 --> 00:03:59.137
Darling replied.

69
00:03:59.157 --> 00:04:02.819
"You are finally home, and that is where you will stay."

70
00:04:02.839 --> 00:04:07.521
"But who will look after Peter, and cook and clean for him?"

71
00:04:08.062 --> 00:04:08.722
Wendy asked.

72
00:04:08.742 --> 00:04:11.323
"He does so need a mother."

73
00:04:11.343 --> 00:04:17.086
"So do you, Wendy," said her mother sternly.

74
00:04:18.026 --> 00:04:21.568
But when she saw Peter's mouth tremble, she made him another offer.

75
00:04:22.516 --> 00:04:26.999
She would let Wendy join him for one week every year to help him with his spring cleaning.

76
00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:32.303
Having no sense of time, Peter was very happy with this offer.

77
00:04:33.184 --> 00:04:37.047
But Wendy said sadly, "You won't forget me, Peter, will you?

78
00:04:37.907 --> 00:04:39.869
Before spring cleaning time comes?"

79
00:04:40.789 --> 00:04:42.391
Peter promised to remember her.

80
00:04:43.431 --> 00:04:46.414
And then, in the blink of an eye, he flew away.
